      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database connection is persistently failing with an authentication error, so I cannot execute verification queries. I'll rely on the strong semantic-network evidence and precedent metric SQL gathered above, and complete the report.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (Phase 1 survivors relevant to the task):**\n\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term. Key columns: `TERM_CODE` (YYYYTT), `SUBJECT_ID`, `COURSE_NUMBER` (\"joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER and SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE\"), `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` (\"joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"), `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (\"Number of students enrolled in the subject\"), `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER`, `TOTAL_UNITS`.\n- **SUBJECT_SUMMARY** — Subject-level summary per term with final enrollment statistics. Has `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `DEPARTMENT_CODE`/`DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` (official registrar enrollment), but **no NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS and no COURSE_NUMBER** column (per retrieved column list).\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Section-level grain (one row per section per term); `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` is per-section, requiring aggregation to subject level.\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — Department dimension: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` ('Y'/'N' **department**-level flag).\n- **SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION** — Catalog course descriptions: `COURSE` (\"joins to … COURSE_NUMBER\"), `DEPARTMENT`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` (\"'Y'/'N' flag whether the **course** counts toward a degree\"), `COURSE_LEVEL`.\n- **STUDENT_DEPARTMENT** — Lighter department lookup (code/name/full name/school); no degree-granting flag.\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Program-scoped subject offerings (textbook program / library reserve scope only); have `TERM_CODE`, `OFFER_DEPT_*`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, but coverage is limited to their program scopes.\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG** — Catalog feeds with unit/grading attributes; COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED has no enrollment measures (per concept comparison: \"Enrollment measures: None (catalog attributes only)\").\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS / ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL / ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER** — Term dimensions; not needed since the term is given as a literal code '2014FA'.\n- **SIS_SUBJECT_CODE** — Subject-code lookup (code↔course number↔department).\n\n**Column concepts:** `column_concept_enrollment_measures`, `column_concept_department_name`, `column_concept_term_code`, `column_concept_subject_id`, `column_concept_master_subject_id`, `column_concept_total_units` (retrieved in full for the first three).\n\n**Concepts:** `concept_subject_offering_facts`, `concept_department_dimension` (retrieved in full).\n\n**Metrics (precedents):** dw_4234, dw_3237, dw_2335, dw_1692, dw_1766, dw_3163, dw_2924, dw_4683, dw_4812 (SQL retrieved for all).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY graph neighbors (retrieved): joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT (outgoing), SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION (outgoing), SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED (incoming, section child), LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, ACADEMIC_TERMS; member of `concept_subject_offering_facts`; columns in `column_concept_term_code`, `column_concept_subject_id`, `column_concept_department_name`, `column_concept_enrollment_measures`, `column_concept_total_units`, `column_concept_master_subject_id`.\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION supports 44 metrics (retrieved via metrics_by_table), including degree-granting course analyses (dw_1766, dw_2924, dw_3163, dw_2335, dw_1692, dw_4234).\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT belongs to `concept_department_dimension`; documented join: `DEPARTMENT_CODE = offering tables' DEPARTMENT_CODE/OFFER_DEPT_CODE`.\n- Documented join in SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION column defs: `COURSE` joins `COURSE_NUMBER`; precedent dw_4234 inner_cte2 uses exactly `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION t0 JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY t1 ON t0.COURSE = t1.COURSE_NUMBER`.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (candidates for \"subjects offered in 2014FA with >5 enrolled students\"):**\n\n| Dimension | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | SUBJECT_SUMMARY | SUBJECT_OFFERED | TIP/LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | subject per term (evidence: table desc) | subject/cluster per term (desc) | section per term (desc) | subject per term, program scope (desc) | catalog record per term (desc) |\n| Enrollment measure | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS + SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (columns) | SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER only (columns) | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS at **section** grain (columns) | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, program-scope snapshot (concept comparison) | **None** (concept comparison) |\n| COURSE_NUMBER for join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE | Yes (column def explicitly documents this join) | **No** such column (retrieved column list) | Yes | Yes | SUBJECT_CODE/SUBJECT_NUMBER instead |\n| Coverage | All registrar subject offerings | All subjects | All sections | Only textbook-program / library-reserve scope (concept comparison: \"may not cover all subjects\") | Catalog attributes only |\n| Fan-out risk | 1 row per subject | 1 row per subject/cluster | Multiple sections per subject → overcount | Program scope gaps | No enrollment |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping:**\n\nAtomic requirements: (R1) term filter '2014FA'; (R2) per-subject enrollment measure with threshold >5; (R3) \"degree-granting **subjects**\" flag; (R4) department name output; (R5) count of subjects per department.\n\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY: R1 SUPPORTED (TERM_CODE), R2 SUPPORTED (NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS at subject grain), R3 SUPPORTED via COURSE_NUMBER→SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE join (documented in column def; precedent dw_4234), R4 SUPPORTED (OFFER_DEPT_CODE→SIS_DEPARTMENT), R5 SUPPORTED (SUBJECT_ID; precedent dw_4234 COUNT(DISTINCT SUBJECT_ID)).\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY: R1 SUPPORTED, R2 partially (only SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, not \"enrolled students\" headcount), R3 **NOT-SUPPORTED directly** (no COURSE_NUMBER column to join SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION; would need SUBJECT_ID string parsing), R4/R5 SUPPORTED.\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED: R2 VIOLATES grain (section-level NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS would double-count subjects with multiple sections unless aggregated).\n- TIP/LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED: R1/R2 SUPPORTED but coverage VIOLATES \"subjects it offered\" (program scope only, per concept comparison).\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: R2 NOT-SUPPORTED (no enrollment measures).\n\n**Degree-granting flag ambiguity:** SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = department-level flag; SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = course/subject-level flag (\"whether the course counts toward a degree\"). The question says \"degree-granting **subjects**\", which lexically matches the subject/course-level flag in SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION. Precedents dw_1766/dw_3163/dw_2335/dw_1692/dw_2924 all use `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'` for \"degree-granting course/subject\" wording; precedents dw_3237/dw_4234 use `SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'` for \"degree-granting **department**\" wording.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"degree-granting subjects\" → SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' (subject-level); excludes the department-level SIS_DEPARTMENT flag by wording (\"subjects\", not \"departments\").\n- \"subjects it offered in the term '2014FA'\" → SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE='2014FA' (registrar offering record, subject grain).\n- \"more than 5 students enrolled\" → NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 5 (decision_guide: \"Questions about number of enrolled students per subject offering … Use NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS from SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject grain)\").\n- \"department name\" → SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME